From cbd3a88d0c36cbdfaafa11987aeaaccb73c63ffa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CharlyRien <9572419+CharlyRien@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 11:57:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 20/23] Lab: tests that touch process-wide lab state are
 serialized (review item 6)

Tests that flip a process-wide lab switch, swap or hold the sparse
STATE, or read counters other tests move now hold
sparse::lab_test_lock (cargo runs tests in parallel; the switch tests
and the STATE swaps of the v2 test could take each other's state). The
Map copy fence left set by MapCopy::new / map_copy_submit is put back
to none after each test that sets it (MapCopyReset), so a later unmap
on another test's device does not wait on it. Tests only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 crates/xcl/src/hle/d3d12x/sparse.rs | 32 +++++++++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/crates/xcl/src/hle/d3d12x/sparse.rs b/crates/xcl/src/hle/d3d12x/sparse.rs
index 2caeb4e5..da5538c5 100644
--- a/crates/xcl/src/hle/d3d12x/sparse.rs
